4fec"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":10,"english":"O foremost of monkeys, there is one, named Maya, spreader of illusions. By him has this entire golden grove been constructed through his wonderful power of construction.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c7a5694fcd93be8d8fcee07f61546acd2e1be9f27e484f49880bdb8d7035e3f","compact":"f95fe3a829bb6692674e7ff23815159a78be9acf73ca166e65202e5ecf9dc40e","nasal":"ea0d95ea5f4c35efd780eefa3445009104ced054acff15c1cec6a53698a7f1e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":11,"english":"He that as reared this excellent golden grove, and this charming mansion, was formerly the Viśvakarmā* of the principal Dänavas. *The name of the celestial architect.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e23493f995263b735c1c8b8d5f5ea862f54d326e22cdfc17b70dc24d84d6df4b","compact":"9e6b6ea6e627da796ec761b3ab09125f8456275d0a6c0507d35503adf8479e65","nasal":"65c89c6c4be6950c229335d2169dd53bcc7f19bf0c4d77164442134386c00152"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":12,"english":"Having for a thousand years thousand years practised austerities in this vast forest, he obtained a boon from the Great-father,-in virtue of which he had attained consummate mastery in his art, as well as absolute control over the materials required therein.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.727,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e24a297d12136e70d6d635d9e622f1b7721480851c2efd10190670016d93850","compact":"00c21d02b68a95f935473292aa538ea6b005e165e24f951cacb9b44b4700fbe2","nasal":"00c21d02b68a95f935473292aa538ea6b005e165e24f951cacb9b44b4700fbe2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":13,"english":"Having accomplished everything, that powerful one, commanding every enjoyment, for a time happily dwelt in this mighty forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"60fa6d7bdd3f9eff0cb5b248c4552310583d0f7c2d14f4388af1a4957c8e798d","compact":"91703b1ae36b55beba3576623e9dbdd501d3d6f4a86515f13fe6fe6b66be6950","nasal":"91703b1ae36b55beba3576623e9dbdd501d3d6f4a86515f13fe6fe6b66be6950"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":14,"english":"Then he, happening to conceive a passion for an Apsara, Hema (by name), Purandara, vigorously wielding his thunder-bolt, struck him dead.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d3b13f7d38ed67eda16d964e5bf89aeb074c0ac30943cd0504424d2951a650ad","compact":"42cc25942745c9a0fec6fa0d3c0f48d4ed197f25cdc7e56c339aafbca836830b","nasal":"42cc25942745c9a0fec6fa0d3c0f48d4ed197f25cdc7e56c339aafbca836830b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":15,"english":"Then Brahmä conferred on Hemā this fine forest and this golden mansion, with the perpetual privilege of enjoying every pleasure herein.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1dca9778089a5eaf2163924960af5a53b2ac77ffed7e76627b93b02f9a8dddca","compact":"838c7618c61b4bdba9e99c40ebaaf334d8b5b25f51d5164858f8fd7595f9c348","nasal":"838c7618c61b4bdba9e99c40ebaaf334d8b5b25f51d5164858f8fd7595f9c348"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":16,"english":"I, Svayamprabhā by name,-the daughter of Merusāvarņi, guard this house of Hemā, O foremost of monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b8a8b0552500daf22b69e6e3452c6897266f3ad0b7471a94288a0010bb754b9d","compact":"a6a10729e539947813ab3c06ffc98dcae326d83de6039f6b37a317f95eeda749","nasal":"a6a10729e539947813ab3c06ffc98dcae326d83de6039f6b37a317f95eeda749"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":17,"english":"Hemā, skilled in dance and song, is my dear friend. having received her blessing, I guard this vast forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d93cfc1ef0cabc922fb7b61566116ceb65374783edf0c2e2181969145b1ba2c7","compact":"eb6cf9fe769a95ce96a4beeedf8e58e69089e5663bcae434aba5dfd228638710","nasal":"eb6cf9fe769a95ce96a4beeedf8e58e69089e5663bcae434aba5dfd228638710"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":18,"english":"What is your errand? And why is it that you have arrived at these lone woods? And how have you managed to see this inaccessible forest?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83e1b324cf1e94c37e8295b91e234582ced30ec06d9534026e5d66e1d367d490","compact":"9d6f41497b230161ec075cd77653bd7a10f6af050922f95adde7c43598d809fa","nasal":"4b13cc37d12c9ab3d70742c335b281991c935a2ac185506f15c1b563352e071f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-50-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":50,"verse":19,"english":"Having partaken of these fruits and roots intended for use, and drunk, do you detail all this to me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-51-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4050019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"791e360a37d91e8e541ff83a77d0e998c25a69d2593426c0106d4ecb3e1fb545","compact":"5be61713c693c35fe4d6df6822f195683a6bb2551b51cc2f5e2a23437444ce57","nasal":"5be61713c693c35fe4d6df6822f195683a6bb2551b51cc2f5e2a23437444ce57"}}]
